<title>USA: Video Update completes acquisition.</title>
<headline>Video Update completes acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Video Update Inc, a video rental chain with 381 superstores in North America, said Monday it completed its acquisition of Superior Video, a 27-store video rental chain in British Columbia.</p>
<p>Prior to completion, the deal was approved by Investment Canada.</p>
<p>Video Update has been managing the operations of Superior Video since April 1, 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;As the second largest U.S.-based video retailer in Canada, we look forward to the added operating synergies these 27 new stores add to our business,&quot; Dan Potter, chairman of Video Update said in a statement.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
